From 017f6fa0d1b6a19d04a42a1753c93a5b9300cb4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hoangvu12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:36:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Auto access mode reaches engines from before it

4b983c6c8 added AccessMode::Auto ("auto"). Engines from before it (0.3.7,
and nightlies before it) fail a whole message holding that value: every
ListHarnesses against a device listing Auto failed, so no older device
could create or message chats there. The same held for a chat row's
config and a run request in Auto.

On the wire "auto" no longer goes where they read (zeron_proto::
access_wire): a catalog's accessModes lists only the modes they know,
with autoAccessMode: true beside it; a chat's or a run's access holds
supervised, with autoAccess: true. Old engines ignore the new fields and
run Auto as supervised, the stricter mode every agent with modes honors
(auto-accept-edits is nearer, but an old engine runs a mode its agent
lacks with full access). This build reads both back into the one value,
and still reads a plain "auto". The in-memory Vec<AccessMode> and
AccessMode fields stay as they were (serde flatten; these are only ever
JSON). The agent gate and zgx, which read and write these as raw JSON,
go through the same helpers, so the gate's cap sees Auto and never
writes "auto".
